<pre class="metadata">
Title: IdP Registration API
Shortname: idp-registration
Level: None
Status: CG-DRAFT
Group: fedidcg
Repository: w3c-fedid/idp-registration
URL: https://w3c-fedid.github.io/idp-registration/
Editor: Sam Goto, w3cid 50308, Google Inc. https://google.com, goto@google.com
Abstract: This specification extends the Federated Credential Management API [[FEDCM]] so that
    the user agent can remember the user's handles (e.g. <code>@alice.example</code>), and so that relying parties can request <em>any</em>
    identity provider that issues one of them and belongs to a federation they accept, instead of
    enumerating identity providers. A handle is registered either by the identity provider, with
    the user's permission, or by the user typing it. Handles are parsed and resolved, and the
    relying party receives a verifiable proof that the user controls the handle, as defined by the
    Handle Verification Protocol [[HVP]].
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css no
Default Biblio Display: inline
Text Macro: RP Relying Party
Text Macro: IDP Identity Provider
